;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-5y5.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-5 5)
  title: "The Old Birch"
  intent: "at the foot of the fall, the oldest birch in the wood, hollow, where the moths winter, and the note you followed among them"
  bed: (wind 0.1 water 0.4 chimes 0.4 drone 0.8)
  grid:
  ("####  %=============#####"
   "####  %         ||| #####"
   "####  %         ||| #####"
   "####  %         ||| #####"
   "####  %         ||| #####"
   "                |||      "
   "                |||######"
   "                |||######"
   "#########~~~#############"
   "#########~~~#############"
   "#########################")
  things: ((harmonic at: (17 7) overtone: 3)
           (lantern-moth at: (17 3) count: 8 drawn: 3))
  decor: auto)
;; The foot of the frozen fall, open to the sky: the top row east of the
;; chimney is the Old Birch's crown (branches, which close the edge under the
;; Frozen Fall's floor but let the room draw under the sky). The chimney
;; comes down at columns 4-5
;; between the fall's glass (column 3) and the rough rock (column 6,
;; climbable back up from the floor), from the Frozen Fall above.
;; The Old Birch is the three-wide trunk (columns 16-18, rows 1-7), its
;; hollow at row 6, just above its base; H3 lies at its foot among the moths' cloud.
;; The passage east (row 5, over the rock step at column 19) leads to the
;; Glass Chute's dark chamber and its green stone (the dark room before
;; H3, David 2026-09-27). Carrying only H2 the caves beyond it stay shut.
;; West under the low rock is Snow Hollow (rows 5-7).
